genn8le17ob09re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nWhat does the fortune teller say? \n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le17ob09re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le17ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le17ob09re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le17ob09re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Jerry from New York wants to know, \"why is a broken mirror seven years bad luck?\" <br/><br/>\nI actually know this one. This superstition was created by the Romans who believed that life was supposed to renew again every seven years. Damaging a mirror was viewed the same as damaging one's health. It was thought that this curse could only be corrected in the next seven year cycle."}, {"time": "23000", "image": "engenn8le17ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "This sounds like it would turn into a great excuse not to do anything. <br/><br/>I imagine, these things were said in ancient Rome before the \u201cbroken mirror bad luck\u201d curse:<br/>\n\u201cif I ate less, I would lose more weight\u201d or \u201cif I were younger, I would fight that gladiator.\u201d<br/>\nOr finally, \u201cI would conquer Mongolia if I liked the cold.\u201d and your friends would all laugh at you.\n<br/><br/>\nHowever, with the broken mirror excuse all you have to say is, \u201cI broke a mirror last night, so I guess I can't make the next invasion of Germany. Sorry.\u201d"}, {"time": "54000", "image": "engenn8le17ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Fortunately, with many superstitions, there are some antidotes to counter it. Here are a few:<br/><br/>If you break a mirror you are supposed to throw salt over your shoulder. <br/>\nIf you break a mirror you are supposed to immediately spin around three times in a counter-clockwise direction.  Finally, you should take a piece of the broken mirror and touch a tombstone with it. It is believed that this will lift the curse immediately.\n<br/><br/>\nOr, if you find yourself with a broken mirror,\nbuy another mirror."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Silly Superstitions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Careful With the Mirror"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe or unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le17ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Be Supposed to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + To be + supposed to + verb"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">  You <span class=\"strong\">are supposed to</span> throw salt over your shoulder. <br/>I <span class=\"strong\">am supposed to</span> spin around three times. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Romans who believed that life was supposed to renew again every seven years. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you break a mirror you are supposed to throw salt over your shoulder. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are supposed to immediately spin around three times."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use an active structure when you want the \"doer\" of the action to be the subject. <br/>You use a passive structure when you want the \"receiver\" of the action to be the subject. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Active sentence = The Romans (subject) <span class=\"strong\">created</span> the superstition about the broken mirror."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Passive sentence = The broken mirror superstition (subject) <span class=\"strong\">was created</span> by the Romans.<br/>It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> followed by the past participle. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Simple Present passive form is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "am/are/is + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The curse  <span class=\"strong\">was lifted</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This superstition was created by the Romans."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Damaging a mirror was viewed the same as damaging one's health."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was thought that this curse could only be corrected in the next seven year cycle."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "curse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a difficult time caused by a bad superstition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This curse could be corrected in a seven year cycle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about superstitions."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to conquer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to win in a war"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would conquer any country in winter if I liked the cold."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Mongolia"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a country in Asia, between Russia and China"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I would conquer Mongolia if I liked the cold."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gladiator"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a fighter in shows in ancient Rome"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I were younger, I would fight that gladiator."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "invasion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the entrance in an enemy territory by an army"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't make the next invasion of Germany."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "antidote "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that prevents or works against negative effects"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With many superstitions there are some antidotes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to counter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to oppose; to block"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can counter the broken mirror superstition."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to spin"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to rotate rapidly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're supposed to spin three times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counter-clockwise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in the opposite direction of the movement of the hands of a clock"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Spin in a counter-clockwise direction."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le17ob09aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, write a dialogue about 12-15 sentences long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "One person has just broken a mirror, one person is the fortune teller."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The fortune teller must explain all the bad things that can happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what your partner is supposed to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The fortune teller must also offer a possible antidote to reverse the curse."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give advice using \u201cIf I were you ... \u201c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change partners."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can talk about things I was supposed to do and things that were supposed to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can talk about hypothetical situations."}]}]}